{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":33005374,"ns":0,"title":"Angelescu polynomials","extract":"In mathematics, the Angelescu polynomials πn(x) are a series of polynomials generalizing the Laguerre polynomials introduced by Aurel Angelescu. The polynomials can be given by the generating function\n  \n    \n      \n        ϕ\n        \n          (\n          \n            \n              t\n              \n                1\n                −\n                t\n              \n            \n          \n          )\n        \n        exp\n        ⁡\n        \n          (\n          \n            −\n            \n              \n                \n                  x\n                  t\n                \n                \n                  1\n                  −\n                  t\n                \n              \n            \n          \n          )\n        \n        =\n        \n          ∑\n          \n            n\n            =\n            0\n          \n          \n            ∞\n          \n        \n        \n          π\n          \n            n\n          \n        \n        (\n        x\n        )\n        \n          t\n          \n            n\n          \n        \n        .","description":"Polynomial sequence","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}